{t: Where did Robinson Crusoe go with Friday on Saturday night?}
{st: (Lewis, Young, Meyer), 1916;}
{st: performed by Al Jolson; Ian Whitcomb, 1966}
{define: Caug7 frets 1 0 0 1}

{textcolour: blue}
Intro:
[F] [D7] [G7] [C7]
{textcolour}

[F] Thousands of years ago, [D7] may-[G7]be [C7]more
[F] Out on an island on a [D7] south-[G7] ern [C7] shore
[D7] Robinson Crusoe landed [G7] one fine day
No rent to pay and no [C7] wife to o- [Caug7] bey

[F] His good man Friday was his [D7] on-[G7] ly [C7] friend
[F7] They didn't borrow or [Bb] lend
[G7] They built a little hut; lived there till Friday, but
Saturday night it was [C7] shut [Caug7]

So, [F] where did Robinson [D7] Crusoe go
With [G7] Friday on Saturday night?
Every [C7] Saturday night they would start in to roam
[G7] And on Sunday morning they'd come [C7] staggering [Caug7] home

On an [D7] island with wild men and cannibal trimmins,
Where [G7] there are wild men,
there [C7] must be wild [Caug7] women
Now, [F] where did Robinson [D7] Crusoe go
With [G7] Friday on [C7] Saturday [F] night? [C7]

{textcolour: blue}
So, [F] where did Robinson [D7] Crusoe go
With [G7] Friday on Saturday night?
Every [C7] Saturday night they would start in to roam
[G7] And on Sunday morning they'd come [C7] staggering home
On an [D7] island with wild men and cannibal trimmins,
Where [G7] there are wild men,
there [C7] must be wild [Caug7] women
Now, [F] where did Robinson [D7] Crusoe go
With [G7] Friday on [C7] Saturday [F] night?
